      "docs": {
        "contents": "Two packages each declare an `interface types`, and this one reaches into\nthe other. Resolving `use test:clocks/monotonic-clock` recurses into that\ninterface's own `use types.{duration}` — an unqualified name that must mean\n`test:clocks/types`, not the `types` being resolved here. Picking the\nnearest same-named interface on the scope stack instead makes the two look\nmutually dependent and reports a false cycle.\n\nThis is the shape WASI p3 uses: `wasi:clocks` and `wasi:sockets` both\ndeclare `interface types`."
      },
